# ConvoKit/Oyez historical corpus source files — immutable local source files,
# not tracked in git. These are operator-supplied inputs to the Phase 29
# historical-corpus importer (utterances.jsonl, conversations.json,
# speakers.json, cases.jsonl, and the justices tenure CSV).
#
# utterances.jsonl alone is ~900MB — GitHub hard-blocks any file over 100MiB,
# so it (and its siblings) must never be `git add`-ed. Only .gitkeep and this
# .gitignore are tracked so the directory exists in the repository.
*.jsonl
*.json
*.csv

# EXCEPTION — justice_identity_mapping.csv is NOT one of the above.
#
# The blanket rules above exist for the ConvoKit/Oyez source files, which are
# operator-supplied and far too large for git (utterances.jsonl alone is ~900MB).
# justice_identity_mapping.csv is neither: it is a 6KB *derived, hand-verified*
# artifact produced during Phase 52-01, and the `*.csv` rule swept it up by
# accident.
#
# It must be tracked, because:
#   1. reset_to_fixture's pre-flight hard-requires it (api/services/admin_dev.py,
#      _require_corpus_files) — without it in the repo, a fresh clone cannot build
#      the fixture at all.
#   2. NOTHING regenerates it. import_justices_csv.py consumes it and
#      pipeline/tests/test_justice_identity_mapping.py validates it; no generator
#      exists, and 52-01 recorded that the middle-initial reconstruction rule was
#      deliberately rejected as a source of truth (88% accurate) and reused only
#      as a verifier.
#   3. Four rows carry operator judgment no matching logic can reproduce — the two
#      Harlans, Salmon P. Chase and Henry Brockholst Livingston were resolved by
#      hand from tenure-date evidence (52-CONTEXT.md D-01).
#
# Losing this file means redoing that hand-resolution. CLAUDE.md's "all derived
# data can be regenerated" does not hold for it, so git is where it lives.
!justice_identity_mapping.csv
